WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.536 --> 00:00:08.058
Dick and Mr.

2
00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:16.520
Hobbs weren't the only ones surprised by the arrival of a new Lord Fauntleroy.

3
00:00:17.741 --> 00:00:21.842
Everyone who lived in or around Dorincourt Castle was talking about it.

4
00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.503
The earl, Mr.

5
00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:28.144
Havisham, and the servants all had opinions about the situation.

6
00:00:29.468 --> 00:00:32.851
Everyone hoped that Cedric would prove to be the real heir.

7
00:00:35.093 --> 00:00:39.076
Out in the stables, Wilkins groomed Cedric's pony with extra care.

8
00:00:39.096 --> 00:00:46.222
"It'll be a sad day if that young man no longer comes to the stables," he said to

9
00:00:46.262 --> 00:00:46.762
the pony.

10
00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:53.948
Of course Cedric had some questions, but he waited awhile to ask the earl.

11
00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.389
One afternoon, as they sat in the library, Cedric decided to speak up.

12
00:01:01.549 --> 00:01:07.892
"This new Lord Fauntleroy and his mother—will they take Mama's house and carriage?"

13
00:01:07.912 --> 00:01:13.315
"No! They can take nothing from her," the earl said firmly.

14
00:01:15.976 --> 00:01:17.037
Cedric exhaled.

15
00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:19.178
"That's a relief.

16
00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:23.240
I wouldn't want her to lose her home or her carriage."

17
00:01:24.944 --> 00:01:28.867
Cedric had to work up his courage to ask another important question.

18
00:01:28.887 --> 00:01:39.173
"That other boy I mean I guess he'll take my place in your life."

19
00:01:40.774 --> 00:01:45.877
"Never!" The earl spoke so fiercely and loudly that Cedric was startled.

20
00:01:45.897 --> 00:01:47.538
"He won't?

21
00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:56.090
I mean, I thought—" Cedric jumped up from his chair and went to his grandfather's side.

22
00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.033
"Do you mean I'll still be your boy?"

23
00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.934
"My boy!"

24
00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:05.516
The earl started to speak, but his voice was shaking.

25
00:02:05.536 --> 00:02:09.578
"Yes, you'll be my boy forever.

26
00:02:10.559 --> 00:02:13.701
Sometimes I feel as if you were the only boy I've ever had."

27
00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.963
Cedric broke into a wide grin.

28
00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:19.004
"Do you mean that?

29
00:02:19.768 --> 00:02:22.089
Then I don't care whether I'm an earl or not."

30
00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.891
The earl laid a hand on Cedric's shoulder.

31
00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:29.932
"I refuse to believe that they can take anything from you.

32
00:02:30.993 --> 00:02:32.674
Or that you can be taken away from me."

33
00:02:33.994 --> 00:02:36.175
Cedric hugged his grandfather tightly.

34
00:02:37.396 --> 00:02:40.137
The old man's eyes were wet with tears.

35
00:02:42.178 --> 00:02:46.980
The earl had refused to meet the woman who claimed her son was the real Lord Fauntleroy.

36
00:02:49.612 --> 00:02:52.314
But one day she arrived at the castle with the boy.

37
00:02:53.615 --> 00:02:56.037
At the door she was told by a footman to wait.

38
00:02:57.518 --> 00:02:59.779
A few minutes later, the footman returned.

39
00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:02.321
"The earl refuses to see you.

40
00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.262
Go away."

41
00:03:05.543 --> 00:03:08.165
The woman looked half-frightened, half-shocked.

42
00:03:09.847 --> 00:03:10.587
But she left.

43
00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:17.132
"I didn't even let her in the door," the footman proudly told the other servants.

44
00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.361
Later the earl told the story to Mr.

45
00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.141
Havisham, who had come for lunch.

46
00:03:23.161 --> 00:03:25.802
"The nerve of that woman!"

47
00:03:26.862 --> 00:03:29.583
The earl buttered his roll with unusual ferocity.

48
00:03:29.603 --> 00:03:32.404
"Coming here uninvited!"

49
00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:37.845
"I can understand not wanting to receive her here," Mr.

50
00:03:37.865 --> 00:03:38.765
Havisham said.

51
00:03:38.785 --> 00:03:41.926
"But I do think you should meet her."

52
00:03:44.007 --> 00:03:45.187
The earl harrumphed.

53
00:03:46.387 --> 00:03:51.542
"She's a bad-tempered, rude woman, but she's not as clever as she thinks.

54
00:03:53.082 --> 00:03:57.365
At times she seems almost overwhelmed by the situation."

55
00:03:59.346 --> 00:04:01.067
Mr. Havisham sipped some water.

56
00:04:01.087 --> 00:04:08.891
"I wonder if she thought she could make this outrageous claim, and we would simply agree to everything."

57
00:04:10.332 --> 00:04:12.533
The earl pointed his fork at the lawyer.

58
00:04:12.553 --> 00:04:16.976
"I still don't understand why you want me to meet her."

59
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:22.743
"We need to investigate this situation further," Mr.

60
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:23.684
Havisham said.

61
00:04:23.704 --> 00:04:28.727
"Let's pay her a visit—and see what she does next."

62
00:04:31.989 --> 00:04:34.891
Mr. Havisham went to the inn where the woman was staying.

63
00:04:37.253 --> 00:04:40.515
He and the earl had agreed to meet in the woman's sitting room.

64
00:04:40.535 --> 00:04:45.519
"The earl will be here in a few minutes," Mr.

65
00:04:45.539 --> 00:04:46.900
Havisham said to the woman.

66
00:04:48.008 --> 00:04:51.890
"You should call me Lady Fauntleroy," the woman said.

67
00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:59.315
"I'm pretty sure that's my title now that my son is Lord Fauntleroy, and—" At that moment the

68
00:04:59.435 --> 00:05:00.795
earl stalked into the room.

69
00:05:03.377 --> 00:05:05.758
He towered over the woman as he stared at her.

70
00:05:06.959 --> 00:05:08.800
Mr. Havisham introduced them.

71
00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:15.764
"I was just telling your lawyer here that he should call me Lady Fauntleroy," the woman said.

72
00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:22.224
"There are a number of things I want—" The earl let her talk and make her demands while

73
00:05:22.284 --> 00:05:23.124
he said nothing.

74
00:05:24.665 --> 00:05:26.807
When she was finished, he finally spoke.

75
00:05:28.088 --> 00:05:30.930
"You say that you are my older son's wife.

76
00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:38.955
If you can prove that is true, then the law is on your side—your boy is Lord Fauntleroy.

77
00:05:40.096 --> 00:05:44.119
But I guarantee that this matter will be looked into thoroughly.

78
00:05:44.139 --> 00:05:47.684
And, if necessary, we will fight you in court."

79
00:05:49.065 --> 00:05:51.305
The earl continued to glare at the woman.

80
00:05:51.325 --> 00:05:57.307
"If your claims are true, you will be provided for.

81
00:05:58.387 --> 00:06:02.288
But I want to see nothing of you or your son as long as I live.

82
00:06:03.309 --> 00:06:07.770
My castle and tenants will unfortunately have enough of you after my death."

83
00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:12.011
Then he turned his back on her and stalked from the room.

84
00:06:13.631 --> 00:06:15.672
The woman looked pale and shaken.
